<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valais</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valais is a canton in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> covering the upper valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a>, with Sion as its capital. Ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Sion from 999, it saw the communes of the German-speaking upper valley take power and conquer the French-speaking lower valley from Savoy in 1475. It joined the Swiss Confederation as a canton in 1815.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valais.jpg" alt="Valais" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian David · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ch%C3%A2teau_de_Val%C3%A8re_et_Haut_de_Cry_-_juillet_2022.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
